// AUTHORED BATCH 003 — B1, B2 and C1, neutral-academic register.
//
// Distractor policy: wherever possible the three wrong options come from the
// SAME semantic field as the sentence (properties of water, parts of a
// building, ways of judging a design) rather than from a stock of absurd
// objects. A distractor that belongs to the topic but cannot answer the
// question tests meaning; one that is obviously silly tests nothing.
//
// STATUS: stage 3 only. Not blind-checked, not shippable.
{"target_word": "reliable", "cefr": "B1", "sentence": "The older instrument is slower but far more ______ than the digital version that replaced it.", "correct_answer": "reliable", "distractors": ["courteous", "fluent", "apologetic"], "explanation": "An instrument that can be trusted to give the same result every time is 'reliable', which is the quality the contrast with 'slower but' sets up. Courteous, fluent and apologetic all describe how a person behaves and cannot apply to a measuring instrument.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"target_word": "investigation", "cefr": "B1", "sentence": "A full ______ into the cause of the failure was ordered before the plant reopened.", "correct_answer": "investigation", "distractors": ["donation", "reunion", "banquet"], "explanation": "Something ordered to establish why a failure happened is a formal inquiry, which 'investigation' names. A donation, a reunion and a banquet are all events or gifts, and none of them can be carried out into a cause.", "difficulty_est": 2}
{"target_word": "decline", "cefr": "B1", "sentence": "Researchers recorded a steady ______ in bird numbers across the whole region over twenty years.", "correct_answer": "decline", "distractors": ["celebration", "instruction", "reminder"], "explanation": "Numbers going down gradually over twenty years is a 'decline'. A celebration, an instruction and a reminder are not quantities, so none of them can be measured in bird numbers.", "difficulty_est": 2}
{"target_word": "reasonable", "cefr": "B1", "sentence": "Given the short notice, the fee charged for the emergency repair seemed entirely ______ to us.", "correct_answer": "reasonable", "distractors": ["coastal", "musical", "wooden"], "explanation": "A price that is not too high for the circumstances is 'reasonable', and the short notice is what makes it fair. A fee is a sum of money, so it cannot be coastal, musical or wooden.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"target_word": "maintenance", "cefr": "B1", "sentence": "Regular ______ of the tunnels costs less over time than waiting for a major failure.", "correct_answer": "maintenance", "distractors": ["applause", "rainfall", "photography"], "explanation": "Routine care that prevents a breakdown is 'maintenance', which is why it works out cheaper than repairing a failure. Applause, rainfall and photography do nothing to keep a tunnel in working order.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"target_word": "regulation", "cefr": "B1", "sentence": "A new ______ requires every supplier to report where its raw materials were produced.", "correct_answer": "regulation", "distractors": ["ornament", "aroma", "landscape"], "explanation": "Something that requires companies to do a thing is an official rule, which 'regulation' names. An ornament, an aroma and a landscape have no authority and cannot require anything of anyone.", "difficulty_est": 2}
{"target_word": "accurate", "cefr": "B1", "sentence": "The early maps were beautifully drawn but far less ______ than modern satellite surveys are.", "correct_answer": "accurate", "distractors": ["fragrant", "magnetic", "washable"], "explanation": "A map that matches the real world closely is 'accurate', and that is exactly what satellite surveys improve on. Being fragrant, magnetic or washable says nothing about whether a map is correct.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"target_word": "satisfaction", "cefr": "B1", "sentence": "Workers reported much greater ______ with their jobs after the company introduced flexible starting hours.", "correct_answer": "satisfaction", "distractors": ["postage", "scenery", "humidity"], "explanation": "The pleasure people feel about their work is 'satisfaction', which flexible hours would plausibly increase. Postage, scenery and humidity are not feelings and cannot be reported about a job in this way.", "difficulty_est": 2}
{"target_word": "unemployment", "cefr": "B1", "sentence": "Long-term ______ in the northern region fell sharply once the new rail link finally opened.", "correct_answer": "unemployment", "distractors": ["architecture", "cuisine", "folklore"], "explanation": "The number of people without work is 'unemployment', and better transport plausibly reduces it. Architecture, cuisine and folklore are not measurable in a way that could fall when a railway opens.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"target_word": "protection", "cefr": "B1", "sentence": "The thick outer shell offers the seed ______ against both drought and grazing animals.", "correct_answer": "protection", "distractors": ["publicity", "employment", "sympathy"], "explanation": "A hard shell keeps danger away from what is inside, which 'protection against' expresses. Publicity, employment and sympathy are things offered to people, and none of them defends a seed from drought.", "difficulty_est": 2}
{"target_word": "category", "cefr": "B1", "sentence": "Each fossil is placed in a single ______ according to the shape of its teeth.", "correct_answer": "category", "distractors": ["orchard", "harbour", "corridor"], "explanation": "A group that things are sorted into by a shared feature is a 'category'. An orchard, a harbour and a corridor are physical places, and nothing is assigned to them on the basis of tooth shape.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"target_word": "gap", "cefr": "B1", "sentence": "There is still a wide ______ between what the theory predicts and what experiments actually show.", "correct_answer": "gap", "distractors": ["hedge", "balcony", "avenue"], "explanation": "A difference between prediction and result is a 'gap' between them. A hedge, a balcony and an avenue occupy physical space and cannot stand between a theory and an experiment.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"target_word": "era", "cefr": "B1", "sentence": "Historians treat the invention of printing as the beginning of an entirely new ______.", "correct_answer": "era", "distractors": ["appetite", "aroma", "signature"], "explanation": "A long period of history with its own character is an 'era', which is what historians date from printing. An appetite, an aroma and a signature cannot begin a historical period.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"target_word": "inform", "cefr": "B1", "sentence": "Staff must ______ the safety officer immediately whenever a chemical container is found damaged.", "correct_answer": "inform", "distractors": ["embroider", "refrigerate", "applaud"], "explanation": "Telling someone about a problem straight away is what 'inform' means. You cannot embroider, refrigerate or applaud a safety officer in response to a damaged container.", "difficulty_est": 2}
{"target_word": "corporation", "cefr": "B2", "sentence": "The quarry is owned by a ______ registered in another country and pays no local tax.", "correct_answer": "corporation", "distractors": ["landmark", "textbook", "sculpture"], "explanation": "A large company that can be registered abroad and hold property is a 'corporation'. A landmark, a textbook and a sculpture cannot own anything or be registered as a legal body.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"target_word": "evolution", "cefr": "B2", "sentence": "The long ______ of the horse can be traced through fossils found on several continents.", "correct_answer": "evolution", "distractors": ["obedience", "digestion", "vocabulary"], "explanation": "Gradual change in a species over millions of years is its 'evolution', which is what a fossil record shows. Obedience, digestion and vocabulary leave no trace in fossils and cannot be traced across continents.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"target_word": "legislation", "cefr": "B2", "sentence": "Recent ______ obliges landlords to insulate any property before it can be rented out.", "correct_answer": "legislation", "distractors": ["weather", "furniture", "traffic"], "explanation": "Law passed by a parliament is 'legislation', and only law can oblige landlords to do something. Weather, furniture and traffic impose no legal duty on anyone.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"target_word": "bankruptcy", "cefr": "B2", "sentence": "The chain filed for ______ after three years of losses and closed every remaining store.", "correct_answer": "bankruptcy", "distractors": ["retirement", "membership", "citizenship"], "explanation": "A business that cannot pay its debts files for 'bankruptcy', which fits three years of losses and total closure. A company cannot apply for retirement, membership or citizenship in these circumstances.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"target_word": "consensus", "cefr": "B2", "sentence": "Only after hours of argument did a genuine ______ emerge among the members of the committee.", "correct_answer": "consensus", "distractors": ["fragrance", "shortage", "echo"], "explanation": "General agreement reached after long discussion is a 'consensus'. A fragrance, a shortage and an echo are not positions people can hold, so none of them emerges from an argument.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"target_word": "compulsory", "cefr": "B2", "sentence": "Attendance at the safety briefing is ______ for everyone entering the laboratory, including visiting staff.", "correct_answer": "compulsory", "distractors": ["reversible", "translucent", "renewable"], "explanation": "Something nobody may skip is 'compulsory', which the phrase 'for everyone, including visiting staff' makes clear. Attendance is not a physical object, so it cannot be reversible, translucent or renewable.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"target_word": "anonymous", "cefr": "B2", "sentence": "The survey is entirely ______, so no answer can ever be traced back to an individual.", "correct_answer": "anonymous", "distractors": ["vertical", "airborne", "handwritten"], "explanation": "A survey that hides who gave each answer is 'anonymous', which is exactly what the second clause explains. Handwriting would in fact make answers easier to trace, and a survey cannot be vertical or airborne.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"target_word": "genuine", "cefr": "B2", "sentence": "Experts confirmed that the manuscript was ______ and not a nineteenth-century copy as some had claimed.", "correct_answer": "genuine", "distractors": ["illegible", "bilingual", "waterlogged"], "explanation": "The contrast with 'not a copy' requires a word meaning real or original, which is 'genuine'. Being illegible, bilingual or waterlogged has no bearing on whether a document is the original or a later imitation.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"target_word": "infer", "cefr": "B2", "sentence": "From the tools alone archaeologists can ______ a great deal about how the settlement was organised.", "correct_answer": "infer", "distractors": ["postpone", "advertise", "dismantle"], "explanation": "Working something out from indirect evidence is what 'infer' means, and tools are exactly such evidence. You cannot postpone, advertise or dismantle information about how a settlement was organised.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"target_word": "devote", "cefr": "B2", "sentence": "Many early astronomers chose to ______ their entire lives to charting a single region of sky.", "correct_answer": "devote", "distractors": ["restore", "exaggerate", "duplicate"], "explanation": "Giving all your time and effort to one purpose is to 'devote' yourself to it. Nobody can restore, exaggerate or duplicate a life in order to spend it on a task.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"target_word": "penalty", "cefr": "B2", "sentence": "Any team fielding an unregistered player faces an automatic ______ of three competition points.", "correct_answer": "penalty", "distractors": ["upgrade", "refund", "discount"], "explanation": "A punishment imposed for breaking a rule is a 'penalty', and losing points is the punishment here. An upgrade, a refund and a discount are all benefits, so none of them follows from breaking a rule.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"target_word": "species", "cefr": "B2", "sentence": "The island supports at least twelve ______ of beetle found nowhere else on earth.", "correct_answer": "species", "distractors": ["chapters", "portions", "editions"], "explanation": "Distinct kinds of living thing are 'species', which is what can be unique to an island. Chapters, portions and editions divide books or quantities, not populations of insects.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"target_word": "withdrawal", "cefr": "B2", "sentence": "The sudden ______ of foreign funding forced the institute to halt three long-running studies.", "correct_answer": "withdrawal", "distractors": ["translation", "duplication", "decoration"], "explanation": "Money being taken away is a 'withdrawal' of funding, which explains why the studies stopped. Translating, duplicating or decorating funding is meaningless and would not force research to end.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"target_word": "trivial", "cefr": "B2", "sentence": "Most of the objections raised at the hearing were ______ and did not affect the final decision.", "correct_answer": "trivial", "distractors": ["metallic", "nocturnal", "hereditary"], "explanation": "Objections too small to matter are 'trivial', which is why the decision was unchanged. An objection is an argument, so it cannot be metallic, nocturnal or hereditary.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"target_word": "inherent", "cefr": "C1", "sentence": "The risk is ______ in the method itself and cannot be removed by better training alone.", "correct_answer": "inherent", "distractors": ["soluble", "punctual", "luminous"], "explanation": "A danger built into a method and impossible to train away is 'inherent' in it. A risk is not a substance or a person, so it cannot be soluble, punctual or luminous.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"target_word": "alleviate", "cefr": "C1", "sentence": "Simple painkillers can ______ the worst of the symptoms but do nothing about the underlying cause.", "correct_answer": "alleviate", "distractors": ["itemise", "narrate", "inherit"], "explanation": "Making suffering less severe without curing it is what 'alleviate' means, which the contrast with the underlying cause demands. Painkillers cannot itemise, narrate or inherit symptoms.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"target_word": "constraint", "cefr": "C1", "sentence": "Time was the only real ______ on the project, since money and staff were both plentiful.", "correct_answer": "constraint", "distractors": ["tribute", "verdict", "postscript"], "explanation": "A limit on what a project can do is a 'constraint' on it, and the second clause rules out the other two possible limits. A tribute, a verdict and a postscript place no restriction on how work proceeds.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"target_word": "credibility", "cefr": "C1", "sentence": "Repeated errors in the earlier report damaged the author's ______ long before the final version appeared.", "correct_answer": "credibility", "distractors": ["eyesight", "handwriting", "posture"], "explanation": "Mistakes make readers less willing to believe a writer, and that trust is 'credibility'. Errors in a report cannot damage an author's eyesight, handwriting or posture.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"target_word": "obscure", "cefr": "C1", "sentence": "Heavy editing tended to ______ rather than clarify what the original writer had actually meant.", "correct_answer": "obscure", "distractors": ["celebrate", "italicise", "punctuate"], "explanation": "The contrast with 'clarify' calls for a verb meaning to make harder to understand, which is 'obscure'. Celebrating, italicising or punctuating a meaning is not the opposite of clarifying it.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"target_word": "spontaneous", "cefr": "C1", "sentence": "The applause was entirely ______, since nobody had arranged for the audience to react that way.", "correct_answer": "spontaneous", "distractors": ["nutritional", "microscopic", "aquatic"], "explanation": "A reaction that happens by itself with no planning is 'spontaneous', which the second clause spells out. Applause is a sound made by people and cannot be nutritional, microscopic or aquatic.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"target_word": "tedious", "cefr": "C1", "sentence": "Copying thousands of figures by hand was ______ work that nobody in the department volunteered for.", "correct_answer": "tedious", "distractors": ["seasonal", "aerial", "ceremonial"], "explanation": "Long, repetitive work that people avoid is 'tedious'. Copying figures at a desk is not seasonal, aerial or ceremonial, so none of those explains why nobody wanted the job.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"target_word": "oversee", "cefr": "C1", "sentence": "A single inspector was appointed to ______ every stage of the building work in the district.", "correct_answer": "oversee", "distractors": ["demolish", "illustrate", "publicise"], "explanation": "Watching over work to make sure it is done properly is what an inspector does, and 'oversee' names it. An inspector is not appointed to demolish, illustrate or publicise the stages of a building project.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"target_word": "circulation", "cefr": "C1", "sentence": "Poor ______ of air in the deep mine allowed dust to build up to dangerous levels.", "correct_answer": "circulation", "distractors": ["ownership", "pronunciation", "cultivation"], "explanation": "Air that does not move around freely has poor 'circulation', which is why dust collects. Air cannot have ownership, pronunciation or cultivation, so none of the others explains the build-up.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"target_word": "divergence", "cefr": "C1", "sentence": "A slight ______ between the two sets of measurements grew larger with every additional trial.", "correct_answer": "divergence", "distractors": ["partnership", "handshake", "rivalry"], "explanation": "Two results moving steadily further apart show a growing 'divergence' between them. Sets of measurements cannot form a partnership, exchange a handshake or develop a rivalry.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"target_word": "durable", "cefr": "C1", "sentence": "The coating proved surprisingly ______, surviving ten winters without cracking or losing its colour.", "correct_answer": "durable", "distractors": ["talkative", "aromatic", "buoyant"], "explanation": "Something that lasts for years without damage is 'durable', which the ten winters demonstrate. Surviving winters intact says nothing about whether a coating is talkative, aromatic or buoyant.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"target_word": "expire", "cefr": "C1", "sentence": "Permits granted under the old system will ______ at the end of next month without exception.", "correct_answer": "expire", "distractors": ["hibernate", "germinate", "migrate"], "explanation": "A document that stops being valid on a fixed date is said to 'expire'. Hibernating, germinating and migrating are things living creatures and plants do, not official permits.", "difficulty_est": 4}
